-- TYPICALLY on a section GIVEN, an ASSUME and a record field, in one exhibit.
--
-- A section GIVEN's or an ASSUME's TYPICALLY lowers exactly as a rule's own
-- GIVEN does (R10, see tariff.l4): the scope variable becomes a Catala `context`
-- with an in-scope `definition` of the default, so a Catala caller may leave it
-- out. A record field cannot be mapped the same way, because a Catala structure
-- has no field defaults: the default is dropped and the notes block says so.
--
-- `rate` (a section GIVEN) is 3 unless a caller says otherwise, `allowance` (an
-- ASSUME) is 100, and `timeout` (a field) is 30 in L4 and nothing in Catala.
--
-- There is no directive: a decision that reads a module-level input cannot be a
-- generated Catala `#[test]` scope (a test scope declares no inputs), and L4 does
-- not evaluate an ASSUME's default, so no L4 oracle exists for this module. Two
-- things pin the mapping instead: tests that read the emitted text, and the
-- hand-written scopes in tests/defaults.catala_en, which etc/validate-catala.mjs
-- appends to a staged copy of the golden and runs under `clerk test`.

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3

ASSUME allowance IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 100

DECLARE Config HAS
    timeout IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 30
    retries IS A NUMBER

@export Budget for a configuration
GIVEN c IS A Config
GIVETH A NUMBER
`budget` c MEANS ((c's timeout) TIMES (c's retries) TIMES rate) PLUS allowance
